You may be waiting too long before trying to escape.  My rule of thumb
is that any non-trivial loss of HP (i.e. more than one or two points)
is a bad thing, and that if I've lost more than 25% of my HP, I'm in
very serious danger and should do anything I can to escape.  If you
wait until you've lost half of your HP, then you're already literally
half dead.

Being surrounded by monsters, however wimpy, is also a danger signal.
Always keep an exit route open, and don't hesitate to teleport
(yourself or the monsters) if necessary to ensure this.  The E-word
can keep most monsters at bay, but should also preferentially be used
_before_ you're surrounded on all sides.

A useful trick is to write the E-word on a choke point, drop an object
on it -- single zorkmids are convenient for this -- and retreat.  The
monsters will stay on the other side while you beat it to safety.  You
may also want to use a hard gem or ring to engrave it in advance; this
will take more turns, but it'll last longer too.  Jumping boots can be
very useful for skipping over an E-word without smudging it.

For serious situations, carry a wand of fire or lightning with you.
(One turn to engrave, cannot be smudged.)

